    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d98bbd5d_cbb7be5d",
        "filename": "common/main.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-07T12:57:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, the race window is between line 89 and 94. If we\u0027re hit by the 2nd reset after reset flags are cleared and before HELD_POR is saved, RESET_PIN will be set instead of POWER_ON.",
      "parentUuid": "c7251832_cb95658c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "8e6aaac0de7b97c1de3080a54781ad6a23622deb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e0469c20_b7c8e54a",
        "filename": "common/main.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 97,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-07T02:17:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why this much? If the 2nd reset doesn\u0027t come within 500 msec, what\u0027s the chance it would ever come?\n\nI also think it\u0027s wise to let the system boot instead of making it look like bricked. The side effect of missing POWER_ON doesn\u0027t seem as big as not booting for 80 seconds. We should propagate delayed_reset_failure properly.\n\nOn Puff, a coincell eventually fails? What\u0027s the worst thing which could happen? Do we need to update the AVL (and OEMs)?\n\nNevertheless, we should try not to build critical code around POWER_ON, IMHO.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 97,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 97,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "8e6aaac0de7b97c1de3080a54781ad6a23622deb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
